@host = http://localhost:5000
@subject = dev-user
@tenant = dev
@roles = system_admin

### Readiness — never calls the model, so it is the safe poll
GET {{host}}/alive

### The module is actually loaded. A module that never loads still compiles.
GET {{host}}/api/platform/modules
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### The Requisitions tab's data endpoint
GET {{host}}/api/hiring/requisitions
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### The same endpoint as compliance — MUST be 403. That tier reads impact reports, never candidates.
GET {{host}}/api/hiring/requisitions
X-Dev-Subject: it-compliance
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: hiring-compliance

### The truth about permissions: both registration sites, and the approval flags
GET {{host}}/api/admin/security/catalog
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### A read turn. Expect list_requisitions and NO approval_required.
POST {{host}}/api/agui/hiring
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{ "messages": [ { "id": "m1", "role": "user", "content": "Which requisitions still need a rubric?" } ] }

### A write turn. Expect propose_rubric, CUSTOM(approval_required), and a reply that does NOT
### claim the rubric is approved or usable for screening.
POST {{host}}/api/agui/hiring
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

{ "messages": [ { "id": "m1", "role": "user", "content": "Propose a rubric for REQ-142 from its job description" } ] }

### The same write turn as a sourcer. The tool must never even be offered — RBAC runs before the
### model request is built, so expect NO propose_rubric in the tool calls.
POST {{host}}/api/agui/hiring
Content-Type: application/json
X-Dev-Subject: it-sourcer
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: hiring-sourcer

{ "messages": [ { "id": "m1", "role": "user", "content": "Propose a rubric for REQ-142 from its job description" } ] }

### Pending approvals — where a parked write waits for a human
GET {{host}}/api/chat/approvals
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Tool-call audit — in this product the audit trail is a deliverable, not just a safety net
GET {{host}}/api/admin/audit/tool-calls
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}

### Per-tenant token spend
GET {{host}}/api/admin/usage?days=30
X-Dev-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Dev-Tenant: {{tenant}}
X-Dev-Roles: {{roles}}
